# Mutation cases for "a divergence list nothing opens measures nothing".
#
# Run with
# `scripts/mutate sce-build/tests/mutations/a_list_nothing_opens_measures_nothing.cases`.
#
# `every_declared_divergence_answers_a_real_case` used to require each
# divergence list to declare at least one entry, reasoning that an empty list
# "silently scores that engine perfect". The danger was real and the subject was
# wrong, and the difference is the north star: the plan of record is to retire
# the runtime rewriter, and the terminal state of that work is a divergence list
# with nothing left in it. A gate that fails on the finish line cannot be
# reached — a counter whose zero is forbidden is not a counter.
#
# The non-emptiness was not doing the work either. Each list's suite is red in
# BOTH directions: an undeclared divergence fails, and so does a declared one
# that has been repaired. A list emptied to silence a red run turns the suite
# red from the other side. What neither direction catches is a list nothing
# OPENS any more — then the suite measures nothing and whatever the file says
# scores the engine perfect. So that is what the gate checks now, empty list or
# not, and these cases are what say it can fail.
#
# The second case is the boundary, and it is the same one this repository has
# now paid for three times in three languages: a file NAMED is not a file
# OPENED. `EcmaScriptSemanticsTest.cpp` prints the list's path twice to tell an
# author where to edit, so a sweep that accepted any mention would take a
# diagnostic ABOUT the file as proof that the file is still opened.

mutation_tests -p sce-build --test ecma262_scoreboard_contract
mutation_targets sce-build/tests/ecma262_scoreboard_contract.rs
# Read at run time: the binding the C++ suite reaches the list through is a
# compile definition in a CMake file the test opens by path.
mutation_runtime_targets tests/CMakeLists.txt

mutation_case "the suite's binding of the divergence list is redirected" <<'PY'
edit("tests/CMakeLists.txt",
     'SCE_LUA_DIVERGENCES_PATH="${CMAKE_SOURCE_DIR}/tests/ecmascript/lua_engine_divergences.json"',
     'SCE_LUA_DIVERGENCES_PATH="${CMAKE_SOURCE_DIR}/tests/ecmascript/divergences_moved.json"')
PY

mutation_case "a path merely mentioned is counted as a path opened" <<'PY'
edit("sce-build/tests/ecma262_scoreboard_contract.rs",
     "        Some(at) => code[..at].contains('='),",
     "        Some(at) => at < code.len(),")
PY
